      "code": "link_to(\"View Invoice\", Order.includes(:user).find(params[:id]).stripe_hosted_invoice_url, :target => \"_blank\", :rel => \"noopener\", :class => \"text-red-600\")",
      "render_path": null,
      "location": null,
      "user_input": "Order.includes(:user).find(params[:id]).stripe_hosted_invoice_url",
      "confidence": "Weak",
      "note": "Explicitly acknowledged and accepted by the project owner (2026-07-20). Unlike the stripe_dashboard_*_url entries above, stripe_hosted_invoice_url is not built from a hardcoded prefix by our own code — it's stored verbatim from Stripe::Invoice#hosted_invoice_url, a real field on Stripe's own API response (see Payments::WebhookHandler#hosted_invoice_url_for). It is still never user-settable: it's written exclusively inside handle_completed, only reachable after Stripe's own webhook signature verification, from a value Stripe's API itself returns — never from params or any form input. Re-review if this column is ever populated from any other source."
